# Enterprise Static Routing & VLAN Network Topology (Cisco Packet Tracer)

A comprehensive enterprise network simulation built in Cisco Packet Tracer, demonstrating multi-VLAN segmentation, inter-VLAN routing, and robust Static Routing configuration across multiple interconnected routers and switches.

---

## 🚀 Project Overview
This project simulates a structured multi-department enterprise network layout. It implements strict network segmentation using VLANs to optimize broadcast domains and security, alongside manual static routing tables to ensure seamless end-to-end communication across different subnets.

---

## 🛠️ Network Architecture & Design

### 1. VLAN Configuration & Segmentation
* VLAN 10: Sales
* VLAN 20: Stocks
* VLAN 30: HR
* VLAN 40: Boss / Management
* VLAN 50: Finance

### 2. Subnetting & Addressing Scheme
* Subnets Used: 
  * 192.168.10.0/24 (Sales)
  * 192.168.20.0/24 (Stocks)
  * 192.168.30.0/24 (HR)
  * 192.168.40.0/24 (Boss)
  * 192.168.50.0/24 (Finance)
  * Point-to-Point serial/Gigabit links interconnecting core and distribution routers (e.g., 10.0.0.0/30 core backbone).

### 3. Key Technologies & Protocols
* Routing: Static Routing (Manual Route Configuration for inter-subnet reachability).
* Switching: Access and Trunk ports, VLAN configuration, Spanning Tree concepts.
* Simulation Tool: Cisco Packet Tracer (.pkt).

---

## 📂 Repository Contents
* static_routing.pkt — The main Cisco Packet Tracer simulation file.
* README.md — Project documentation and architecture guide.

---

